TI  - Generalized postpartum seizures and posterior reversible encephalopathy syndrome
T2  - GYNAKOLOGE
AB  - An 18-year-old primigravida was admitted to hospital at 41 weeks of gestation. She had gestational diabetes and hereditary thrombophilia. Delivery of the baby was by emergency C-section because of fetal bradycardia. The patient experienced postpartum spontaneous, general seizures. Computed tomography imaging showed no sign of intracerebral hemorrhage or sinus thrombosis. Posterior reversible leukoencephalopathy syndrome was diagnosed, which is often seen in patients with preeclampsia or eclampsia. Our patient, however, showed no other symptoms of preeclampsia or gestosis.
